    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Feature request: Matroska (MKV) video container]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/7347</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/7347"/>
        <updated>2025-12-27T04:31:27.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33988779?u=5b5fc67c907002674087c98a6503db95c41b6245&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">I would like to request a feature for the use of the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matroska" rel="nofollow">Matroska video container</a> (also called MKV) in <code class="notranslate">&lt;video&gt;</code> tags.</p>
<p dir="auto">From my testing, it is supported in the latest versions of Chromium and GNOME Web (WebKit-based), but not in the latest version of Firefox.</p>
<p dir="auto">WebM is based on MKV, but they are not the same format - WebM is already provided as a feature on caniuse.com, and support is present in latest versions of all major browsers.</p>
<p dir="auto">Here's a page I made so I could test support myself: <a href="https://grzesiek11.stary.pc.pl/files/random/mkv.html" rel="nofollow">https://grzesiek11.stary.pc.pl/files/random/mkv.html</a>. From top to bottom, this is:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>MP4 with H.264 + AAC</li>
<li>WebM with AV1 + Opus</li>
<li>Matroska with AV1 + Opus</li>
<li>Matroska with H.264 + AAC</li>
</ul>]]></content>
